nVulnerability Vmscape:                   Mitigation; IBPB before exit to userspace\n\n==============================\nVersions of relevant libraries\n==============================\n[pip3] flashinfer-python==0.7.0.post1\n[pip3] nccl-extensions==0.1.0\n[pip3] nccl4py==0.6.0\n[pip3] numpy==2.3.5\n[pip3] nvidia-cublas==13.1.1.3\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-cccl==13.3.3.3.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-crt==13.3.33\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-cupti==13.0.85\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvcc==13.2.78\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvdisasm==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvrtc==13.0.88\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-runtime==13.0.96\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-tileiras==13.2.78\n[pip3] nvidia-cudnn-cu13==9.20.0.48\n[pip3] nvidia-cudnn-frontend==1.30.0\n[pip3] nvidia-cufft==12.0.0.61\n[pip3] nvidia-cufile==1.15.1.6\n[pip3] nvidia-curand==10.4.0.35\n[pip3] nvidia-cusolver==12.0.4.66\n[pip3] nvidia-cusparse==12.6.3.3\n[pip3] nvidia-cusparselt-cu13==0.8.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-base==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-core==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu12==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu13==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-ml-py==13.610.43\n[pip3] nvidia-nccl-cu13==2.29.7\n[pip3] nvidia-nvjitlink==13.0.88\n[pip3] nvidia-nvshmem-cu13==3.4.5\n[pip3] nvidia-nvtx==13.0.85\n[pip3] nvidia-nvvm==13.2.78\n[pip3] optree==0.19.1\n[pip3] pyzmq==27.1.0\n[pip3] tokenspeed-triton==3.7.10.post20260531\n[pip3] torch==2.13.0+cu130\n[pip3] torch_c_dlpack_ext==0.1.5\n[pip3] torchaudio==2.11.0\n[pip3] torchcodec==0.17.0\n[pip3] torchvision==0.28.0\n[pip3] transformers==5.17.0\n[pip3] triton==3.7.1\n[conda] flashinfer-python         0.7.0.post1              pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nccl-extensions           0.1.0                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nccl4py                   0.6.0                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] numpy                     2.3.5                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cublas             13.1.1.3                 pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-cccl          13.3.3.3.1               pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-crt           13.3.33                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-cupti         13.0.85                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-nvcc          13.2.78                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-nvdisasm      13.4.92                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-nvrtc         13.0.88                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-runtime       13.0.96                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cuda-tileiras      13.2.78                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cudnn-cu13         9.20.0.48                pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cudnn-frontend     1.30.0                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cufft              12.0.0.61                pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cufile             1.15.1.6                 pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-curand             10.4.0.35                pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cusolver           12.0.4.66                pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cusparse           12.6.3.3                 pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cusparselt-cu13    0.8.1                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cutlass-dsl        4.7.1                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-base 4.7.1                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-core 4.7.1                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu12 4.7.1                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu13 4.7.1                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-ml-py              13.610.43                pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-nccl-cu13          2.29.7                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-nvjitlink          13.0.88                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-nvshmem-cu13       3.4.5                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-nvtx               13.0.85                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] nvidia-nvvm               13.2.78                  pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] optree                    0.19.1                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] pyzmq                     27.1.0                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] tokenspeed-triton         3.7.10.post20260531          pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] torch                     2.13.0+cu130             pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] torch-c-dlpack-ext        0.1.5                    pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] torchaudio                2.11.0                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] torchcodec                0.17.0                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] torchvision               0.28.0                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] transformers              5.17.0                   pypi_0    pypi\n[conda] triton                    3.7.1                    pypi_0    pypi\n\n==============================\n         vLLM Info\n==============================\nROCM Version                 : Could not collect\nvLLM Version                 : 0.31.0\nvLLM Build Flags:\n  CUDA Archs: Not Set; ROCm: Disabled; XPU: Disabled\nGPU Topology:\n  \t\u001B[4mGPU0\tGPU1\tGPU2\tGPU3\tGPU4\tGPU5\tGPU6\tGPU7\tCPU Affinity\tNUMA Affinity\tGPU NUMA ID\u001B[0m\nGPU0\t X \tNODE\tNODE\tNODE\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\t0-15,32-47\t0\t\tN/A\nGPU1\tNODE\t X \tNODE\tNODE\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\t0-15,32-47\t0\t\tN/A\nGPU2\tNODE\tNODE\t X \tNODE\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\t0-15,32-47\t0\t\tN/A\nGPU3\tNODE\tNODE\tNODE\t X \tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\t0-15,32-47\t0\t\tN/A\nGPU4\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\t X \tNODE\tNODE\tNODE\t16-31,48-63\t1\t\tN/A\nGPU5\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tNODE\t X \tNODE\tNODE\t16-31,48-63\t1\t\tN/A\nGPU6\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tNODE\tNODE\t X \tNODE\t16-31,48-63\t1\t\tN/A\nGPU7\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\tNODE\tNODE\tNODE\t X \t16-31,48-63\t1\t\tN/A\n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\n==============================\n     Environment Variables\n==============================\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/data/zyzhao/anaconda3/envs/tcgp/lib/python3.12/site-packages/cv2/../../lib64:/opt/llvm-17/lib:/data/zyzhao/cuda/lib64:/opt/llvm-17/lib:/data/zyzhao/cuda/lib64:\nCUDA_HOME=/data/zyzhao/cuda\nCUDA_HOME=/data/zyzhao/cuda\nPYTORCH_NVML_BASED_CUDA_CHECK=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_COMPILE_THREADS=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/torchinductor_zyzhao\nVLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn\n```\n\n\n### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\n## Description\n\nOn `LiquidAI/LFM2-8B-A1B` (hybrid conv + SSM + full-attention), **greedy decoding is not reproducible**: with the same engine instance, same seed and same prompts, `temperature=0` produces different token sequences across repeated `generate()` calls. The batch is identical across rounds; the only difference is time (and therefore kernel/scheduling order).\n\nThe divergence signature is consistent across every mismatching prompt: **a long identical prefix, a single differing token, then re-alignment** — the classic signature of a nondeterministic reduction order (atomicAdd / split-K accumulation) perturbing logits just enough to flip an argmax. Measured examples (128 generated tokens per prompt):\n\n```\np0: common prefix 36 tok | A tail=[41677, 856, 21473, 3256, 779, 23981]\n                         | B tail=[41677, 856, 21473,  884, 779, 23981]\np1: common prefix 66 tok | A tail=[523, 3604, 8676, 15637, 779, 2565]\n                         | B tail=[523, 3604, 8676,  2316, 779, 5743]\np3: common prefix 75 tok | A tail=[51197, 11478, 968, 9029, 10222, 3604]\n                         | B tail=[51197, 11478, 968, 12051, 10222, 3604]\n```\n\nRuled out:\n\n- **CUDA graphs**: the mismatch persists with `cudagraph_mode=\"NONE\"` (3 of 4 prompts diverge; one diverges at the very first output token) → not a graph-replay artifact.\n- **Sampling RNG**: `temperature=0` → pure argmax, no sampling noise.\n- **Batch-invariance / cold-start cache state**: the divergence is between two **warm** rounds, not between a cold and a warm one; the warm rounds themselves disagree.\n\nRuled in as **LFM2/hybrid-mamba-specific**: the same probe on `Qwen/Qwen1.5-MoE-A2.7B-Chat` (dense-attention MoE, same machine, same stack) is stable — warm-vs-warm and cold-vs-warm both identical.\n\nImpact: greedy-decode reproducibility is a baseline expectation for evaluation reproducibility and A/B testing; any downstream harness comparing outputs run-to-run on hybrid models sees phantom diffs.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom vllm import LLM, SamplingParams\n\nllm = LLM(\n    model=\"LiquidAI/LFM2-8B-A1B\",\n    max_model_len=4096,\n    seed=42,\n    gpu_memory_utilization=0.85,   # lower if your GPU is smaller\n)\nprompts = [\"The capital of France is\", \"Count from 1 to 10:\"]\nsp = SamplingParams(temperature=0.0, max_tokens=64)\n\nr1 = [list(o.outputs[0].token_ids) for o in llm.generate(prompts, sp)]\nr2 = [list(o.outputs[0].token_ids) for o in llm.generate(prompts, sp)]\nfor i, (a, b) in enumerate(zip(r1, r2)):\n    if a != b:\n        d = next(j for j, (x, y) in enumerate(zip(a, b)) if x != y)\n        print(f\"prompt {i}: diverge at token {d}: {a[d:d+6]} vs {b[d:d+6]}\")\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nTwo consecutive `generate()` calls with identical prompts and `temperature=0` on the same engine return identical token sequences.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nWarm-vs-warm rounds diverge at one or more prompts (see the evidence table below); the divergence persists across repeated rounds and is not removed by disabling CUDA graphs.\n\n## Environment\n\n- vLLM: 0.31.0 (official wheel)\n- PyTorch: 2.13.0+cu130, CUDA 13.0, driver 580.82.07\n- GPU: **按实测填写**（复现时用 `torch.cuda.get_device_capability()` 确认；示例：`NVIDIA RTX A6000, sm86` 或 `NVIDIA RTX 5880 Ada Generation, sm89`）\n- OS: Ubuntu 22.04.4 LTS (glibc 2.35), Python 3.12.13\n- Model: `LiquidAI/LFM2-8B-A1B` (hybrid mamba, bf16 checkpoint)\n\n## Evidence (standalone reproduction, same engine instance, warm-vs-warm comparison)\n\nAll rows below come from `repro_greedy_nondeterminism_lfm2.py` re-run outside the automated pipeline. \"warm-vs-warm\" means two rounds both executed after warmup; a mismatch there cannot be explained by cold-start cache state.\n\n| # | config | warm-vs-warm | cold-vs-warm | note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **B** (primary) | `mamba_cache_dtype=\"float16\"`, `cudagraph_mode=\"NONE\"` | **mismatch 3/4** (p0 p1 p2) | mismatch 2/4 (p1 p2) | CUDA graphs excluded; no `use_fp64_gumbel` |\n| **A** (secondary) | `mamba_cache_dtype=\"float16\"` + `quantization=\"fp8_per_block\"` + `use_fp64_gumbel=True` | **mismatch 4/4** | mismatch 3/4 | see note 4 in the submission note — verify `use_fp64_gumbel` semantics first |\n| control | `Qwen/Qwen1.5-MoE-A2.7B-Chat`, same probe/machine | identical | identical | non-hybrid-attention MoE is stable |\n\nPer-prompt divergence detail for config B (24 generated tokens, `cudagraph_mode=\"NONE\"`):\n\n```\np0: common prefix  2 tok | A=[..., 5242,  523, 3604, 1098,  908]\n                         | B=[..., 5242,  523, 1311,  856, 5408]\np1: common prefix  0 tok | A=[...,  730,  526,  521]\n                         | B=[..., 3604,  526,  521]\np2: common prefix 15 tok | A=[..., 1883,  856, 28027,  797,  768, 32524]\n                         | B=[..., 1883,  856, 28027,  988,  730,  1698]\n```\n\nNote that p1 diverges at the **very first output token** with CUDA graphs disabled — this is the strongest single datapoint that the nondeterminism is not a graph-replay or cache-state artifact.\n\n## Additional context\n\n- Found by an automated warm-vs-warm determinism probe in a config-interaction test generator, then reproduced standalone.\n- Suspect areas (hybrid-mamba-specific kernels): the SSM scan / conv1d update path (`precopy_mamba_align_fused_kernel`, `_causal_conv1d_fwd_kernel`, `_causal_conv1d_update_kernel`, `postprocess_mamba_fused_kernel` under `vllm/v1/worker/mamba_utils.py` and the model's mamba layers) for nondeterministic reductions; secondarily the fused-MoE routing/weighted-sum path if it uses atomics.\n- Related observation, possibly relevant: the same run emits `jit_monitor` warnings for exactly those per-step mamba kernels being JIT-compiled **during inference** (i.e. they are not covered by the startup warmup). Since they are compiled lazily on the first step, any autotuning/scheduling difference between rounds could also contribute to round-to-round numerical differences.\n\n## What is and is not being claimed\n\n- **Claimed**: on LFM2, two `temperature=0` calls on the same engine can return different tokens, violating the usual expectation that greedy decoding is reproducible.\n- **Not claimed**: that this is a specific kernel's bug — the responsible reduction is not yet isolated.\n- **Open item for the harness side** (not a vLLM defect): a determinism probe that compares only *within* a single `generate()` call cannot detect this class of divergence; it needs an explicit \"same engine, two separate calls\" round. That gap is why this was initially mis-bucketed as cold-start noise.\n\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61319/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61337","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61337/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61337/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61337/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61337","id":5825021454,"node_id":"I_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABWzLGDg","number":61337,"title":"[Bug]: DFlash drafter CUDA graph capture fails with FLEX_ATTENTION backend (seq_lens_cpu_upper_bound is None)","user":{"login":"oscarw-td","id":318511979,"node_id":"U_kgDOEvwbaw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/318511979?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td","html_url":"https://github.com/oscarw-td","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5135047172,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABMhKaBA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-13T05:24:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T23:40:52Z","clos