U Info\n==============================\nArchitecture:                            x86_64\nCPU op-mode(s):                          32-bit, 64-bit\nAddress sizes:                           46 bits physical, 57 bits virtual\nByte Order:                              Little Endian\nCPU(s):                                  16\nOn-line CPU(s) list:                     0-15\nVendor ID:                               GenuineIntel\nModel name:                              Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 5418Y\nCPU family:                              6\nModel:                                   143\nThread(s) per core:                      1\nCore(s) per socket:                      8\nSocket(s):                               2\nStepping:                                8\nBogoMIPS:                                4000.00\nFlags:                                   fpu vme de pse tsc msr pae mce cx8 apic sep mtrr pge mca cmov pat pse36 clflush dts mmx fxsr sse sse2 ss ht syscall nx pdpe1gb rdtscp lm arch_perfmon pebs bts rep_good nopl xtopology cpuid tsc_known_freq pni pclmulqdq dtes64 vmx ssse3 fma cx16 pdcm pcid sse4_1 sse4_2 x2apic movbe popcnt tsc_deadline_timer aes xsave avx f16c rdrand hypervisor lahf_lm abm 3dnowprefetch cpuid_fault ssbd ibrs ibpb stibp ibrs_enhanced tpr_shadow flexpriority ept vpid ept_ad fsgsbase tsc_adjust bmi1 avx2 smep bmi2 erms invpcid avx512f avx512dq rdseed adx smap avx512ifma clflushopt clwb avx512cd sha_ni avx512bw avx512vl xsaveopt xsavec xgetbv1 xsaves user_shstk avx_vnni avx512_bf16 wbnoinvd arat vnmi avx512vbmi umip pku ospke waitpkg avx512_vbmi2 gfni vaes vpclmulqdq avx512_vnni avx512_bitalg avx512_vpopcntdq la57 rdpid bus_lock_detect cldemote movdiri movdir64b fsrm md_clear serialize tsxldtrk ibt amx_bf16 avx512_fp16 amx_tile amx_int8 flush_l1d arch_capabilities\nVirtualization:                          VT-x\nHypervisor vendor:                       KVM\nVirtualization type:                     full\nL1d cache:                               512 KiB (16 instances)\nL1i cache:                               512 KiB (16 instances)\nL2 cache:                                64 MiB (16 instances)\nL3 cache:                                32 MiB (2 instances)\nNUMA node(s):                            2\nNUMA node0 CPU(s):                       0-7\nNUMA node1 CPU(s):                       8-15\nVulnerability Gather data sampling:      Not affected\nVulnerability Ghostwrite:                Not affected\nVulnerability Indirect target selection: Not affected\nVulnerability Itlb multihit:             Not affected\nVulnerability L1tf:                      Not affected\nVulnerability Mds:                       Not affected\nVulnerability Meltdown:                  Not affected\nVulnerability Mmio stale data:           Not affected\nVulnerability Old microcode:             Not affected\nVulnerability Reg file data sampling:    Not affected\nVulnerability Retbleed:                  Not affected\nVulnerability Spec rstack overflow:      Not affected\nVulnerability Spec store bypass:         Mitigation; Speculative Store Bypass disabled via prctl\nVulnerability Spectre v1:                Mitigation; usercopy/swapgs barriers and __user pointer sanitization\nVulnerability Spectre v2:                Mitigation; Enhanced / Automatic IBRS; IBPB conditional; PBRSB-eIBRS SW sequence; BHI BHI_DIS_S\nVulnerability Srbds:                     Not affected\nVulnerability Tsa:                       Not affected\nVulnerability Tsx async abort:           Mitigation; TSX disabled\nVulnerability Vmscape:                   Not affected\n\n==============================\nVersions of relevant libraries\n==============================\n[pip3] flashinfer-python==0.7.0.post1\n[pip3] nccl-extensions==0.1.0\n[pip3] nccl4py==0.6.0\n[pip3] numpy==2.4.6\n[pip3] nvidia-cublas==13.1.1.3\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-cccl==13.3.4.3.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-crt==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-cupti==13.0.85\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvcc==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvdisasm==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvrtc==13.0.88\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-runtime==13.0.96\n[pip3] nvidia-cudnn-cu13==9.20.0.48\n[pip3] nvidia-cudnn-frontend==1.30.0\n[pip3] nvidia-cufft==12.0.0.61\n[pip3] nvidia-cufile==1.15.1.6\n[pip3] nvidia-curand==10.4.0.35\n[pip3] nvidia-cusolver==12.0.4.66\n[pip3] nvidia-cusparse==12.6.3.3\n[pip3] nvidia-cusparselt-cu13==0.8.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-base==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-core==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu12==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu13==4.7.1\n[pip3] nvidia-ml-py==13.615.71\n[pip3] nvidia-nccl-cu13==2.29.7\n[pip3] nvidia-nvjitlink==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-nvshmem-cu13==3.4.5\n[pip3] nvidia-nvtx==13.0.85\n[pip3] nvidia-nvvm==13.4.92\n[pip3] pyzmq==27.2.0\n[pip3] tokenspeed-triton==3.8.10.post20260920\n[pip3] torch==2.13.0\n[pip3] torch-c-dlpack-ext==0.1.5\n[pip3] torchaudio==2.11.0\n[pip3] torchcodec==0.17.0\n[pip3] torchvision==0.28.0\n[pip3] transformers==5.17.0\n[pip3] triton==3.7.1\n[conda] No relevant packages\n\n==============================\n         vLLM Info\n==============================\nROCM Version                 : Could not collect\nvLLM Version                 : 0.31.0\nvLLM Build Flags:\n  CUDA Archs: Not Set; ROCm: Disabled; XPU: Disabled\nGPU Topology:\n  \tGPU0\tGPU1\tGPU2\tGPU3\tCPU Affinity\tNUMA Affinity\tGPU NUMA ID\nGPU0\t X \tNV6\tNV6\tNV6\t0-15\t0-1\t\tN/A\nGPU1\tNV6\t X \tNV6\tNV6\t0-15\t0-1\t\tN/A\nGPU2\tNV6\tNV6\t X \tNV6\t0-15\t0-1\t\tN/A\nGPU3\tNV6\tNV6\tNV6\t X \t0-15\t0-1\t\tN/A\n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\n==============================\n     Environment Variables\n==============================\nPYTORCH_NVML_BASED_CUDA_CHECK=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_COMPILE_THREADS=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/torchinductor_oscar\n\n```\n\n</details>\nSame as #61330 .\n\n- vLLM: 0.30.0 (`vllm/vllm-openai:latest`)\n- GPU: NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3\n\n\n### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nRunning the DFlash drafter on `FLEX_ATTENTION` (the workaround for #<issue 1>) works with `--enforce-eager`. With CUDA graphs enabled, though, startup fails during drafter graph capture with an `AssertionError` in FlexAttention's capture code. The DFlash capture path doesn't fill in `seq_lens_cpu_upper_bound`, which FlexAttention requires.\n\n**Command**\n\nRun in the `vllm/vllm-openai:latest` Docker image (vLLM 0.30.0) on a single GPU:\n\n```bash\nvllm serve openai/gpt-oss-20b \\\n  --served-model-name openai/gpt-oss-20b \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.80 \\\n  --max-model-len 8192 \\\n  --max-num-seqs 16 \\\n  --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 \\\n  --speculative-config.method dflash \\\n  --speculative-config.model /path/to/dflash-drafter \\\n  --speculative-config.num_speculative_tokens 15 \\\n  --speculative-config.attention_backend FLEX_ATTENTION\n```\n\nSame drafter as in #61330  (DFlash, created with `speculators train --dry-run`, config attached there). The failure happens while building attention metadata for CUDA graph capture, before the drafter's weights are used, and it reproduces with both the untrained and a trained drafter.\n\n**Traceback** (abridged)\n\n```\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py\", line 1045, in capture_model\n    self.speculator.capture()\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash/speculator.py\", line 155, in capture\n    self.query_cudagraph_manager.capture(\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash/cudagraph.py\", line 121, in capture\n    super().capture(create_forward_fn, progress_bar_desc)\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py\", line 436, in capture\n    forward_fn = create_forward_fn(desc, warmup=True)\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash/cudagraph.py\", line 99, in create_forward_fn\n    attn_state = _prepare_dflash_inputs_to_capture(\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash/cudagraph.py\", line 54, in _prepare_dflash_inputs_to_capture\n    attn_metadata = build_attn_metadata(\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py\", line 481, in build_attn_metadata\n    metadata = attn_metadata_builder.build_for_cudagraph_capture(\nFile \"vllm/v1/attention/backends/flex_attention.py\", line 992, in build_for_cudagraph_capture\n    assert common_attn_metadata.seq_lens_cpu_upper_bound is not None\nAssertionError\n```\n\n### What we tried\n\n| Configuration | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `--enforce-eager` | ✅ Works |\n| `--speculative-config.enforce_eager true` (drafter-only eager, target keeps CUDA graphs) | ❌ Same AssertionError. The drafter-only eager setting doesn't seem to stop drafter graph capture under Model Runner V2. |\n| `--compilation-config.cudagraph_mode NONE` | ✅ Works, but loses the CUDA graph speedup, which removes much of DFlash's benefit. |\n\nSo there are two related problems:\n1. `_prepare_dflash_inputs_to_capture` doesn't set `seq_lens_cpu_upper_bound` when building capture metadata, which FlexAttention requires.\n2. `speculative_config.enforce_eager` is apparently not respected by `capture_model` → `speculator.capture()` in the V2 model runner.\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61337/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61337/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60722","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60722/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60722/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60722/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60722","id":5769201838,"node_id":"I_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABV98Irg","number":60722,"title":"[RFC]: Strcutured Outputs Not Respected When Reasoning Implicitly Ends","user":{"login":"yzong-rh","id":263738792,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7hVqA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263738792?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh","html_url":"https://github.com/yzong-rh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yzong-rh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6467979044,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABgYWHJA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/structured-output","name":"structured-output","color":"4cb782","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6478559908,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABgib6pA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/RFC","name":"RFC","color":"DE9220","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8509281801,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAAB-zFWCQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/tool-calling","name":"tool-calling","color":"C1E8F1","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-08T21:31:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T23:35:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Motivation.\n\nI want to start a discussion on how implicit reasoning end can break structured ouptuts + spec decode.\n\n### Background\n\nFor structured outputs, we only apply constrained decoding after reasoning ends. This is to allow models to reason while constraining the user-visible content.\n\nAt each decode step, the scheduler roughly calls:\n1. `StructuredOutputManager.validate_tokens` to validate the draft tokens need constraining and trim any grammar-invalid tokens\n2. `StructuredOutputManager.grammar_bitmask` to create bitmasks for the draft tokens that need constraining\n3. `StructuredOutputManager.accpet_tokens` to advance grammar FSM over the constrained tokens\n\nThese three methods rely on a `StructuredOutputManager._get_constraint_start` helper to identify when reasoning ends. It returns `reasoning_end_index + 1`\n\n### Implicit Reasoning Ends\n\nReasoning end is usually marked by a special token (e.g. `</think>` for GLM 5.3). However, reasoning can also end implicitly when the model starts emitting content or tool call without closing reasoning first (e.g. `<think> ... <tool_call>` instead of `<think> ... </think><tool_call>`). This presents challenges for strcutured output constraint start detection.\n\n### Issues with Implicit Reasoning Ends\n\nCurrently, `StructuredOutputManager._get_constraint_start` assumes all reasoning end markers are explicit. For example, given `prefix <tool_call> suffix`,\n1. `StructuredOutputManager.validate_tokens` doesn't validate the `<tool_call>`\n2. `StructuredOutputManager.grammar_bitmask` creates bitmasks for `suffix` only\n3. `StructuredOutputManager.accpet_tokens` advances grammar FSM over accepted `suffix` + bonux token only.\n\nThis leads to two issues:\n- I1: `<tool_call>` may not be grammar valid, yet it is unconditionally accepted\n- I2: if a model is required to make a tool call, it will be forced to generate duplicate `<tool_call>` because the grammar isn't aware of the first one #59608\n\n### Fix attempt: Adjust `_get_constraint_start` for implicit reasoning end markers. \n\nA simple fix seems to be to make `_get_constraint_start` return `reasoning_end_index` instead of `reasoning_end_index + 1` for implicit reasoning end markers. `_get_constraint_start` still returns `reasoning_end_index + 1` for explicit reasoning end markers.\n\nGiven `prefix <tool_call> suffix`,\n1. `StructuredOutputManager.validate_tokens` now validates `<tool_call> suffix`\n2. `StructuredOutputManager.grammar_bitmask` creates bitmasks for `<tool_call> suffix`\n3. `StructuredOutputManager.accept_tokens` advances grammar FSM over the accepted `<tool_call> suffix` and bonus token.\n\nThis seems to fix both issues:\n- I1: `<tool_call>` is validated and rejected if grammar-invalid\n- I2: grammar is aware of `<tool_call>`, not duplicate emission needed\n\nHowever, the fix is subtly incorrect: spec decode changes the target model's output distribution:\n- the drafter proposes `prefix <tool_call> suffix`\n- structure outputs sees `<tool_call>` and determines that constraint should start\n- but the target model could reject `<tool_call>`, it could choose to continue reasoning\n- but structured ouputs forces a grammar-valid token to be sampled\nConstraint start was determined by the drafter's output, before target model can accpet or reject it.\n\nThis was implemented in my intial attempt and in #59629\n\n### Correct fix: Distinguish between `grammar_start` and `constraint_start`.\n\nMake `_get_constraint_start` return a tuple of `grammar_start, constraint_start`. For explicit reasoning end markers, `grammar_start == constraint_start`. For implicit end markers, `grammar_start < constraint_start`.\n1. `StructuredOutputManager.validate_tokens` validate from `grammar_start`\n2. `StructuredOutputManager.grammar_bitmask` is aware of tokens from `grammar_start` but only emit bitmasks from `constraint_start`\n3. `StructuredOutputManager.accept_tokens` validate from `grammar_start`\n\nGiven `prefix <tool_call> suffix`,\n1. `StructuredOutputManager.validate_tokens` validates `<tool_call> suffix`\n2. `StructuredOutputManager.grammar_bitmask` creatse bitmasks for `suffix` only\n3. `StructuredOutputManager.accept_tokens` advances grammar FSM over the accepted `<tool_call> suffix` and bonus token.\n\nThis fixes both the issues without affecting the target model's output distribution.\n\nThis was implemented in #59627 and merged.\n\n### Remaining Issues\n\nThe fix is currently limited to engine-based parsers. It also doesn't account for implicit multi-token reasoning end markers (e.g. deepseek_v4) or text-only reasoning end markers (e.g. inkling).\n\nThere's also one more fundamental issue that remains: we can still sample implicit reasoning ends even when they are not grammar-valid.\n\nFor example, suppose the grammar disallows tool calls, the drafts are `reasoning_prefix reasoning_suffix`.\n1. `StructuredOutputManager.validate_tokens` doesn't validate anything since reasoning has not ended\n2. `StructuredOutputManager.grammar_bitmask` doesn't constrain anything\n3. Target model rejects `reasoning_suffix`. Since there's no constraint, it can sample `<tool_call>`.\n4. `StructuredOutputManager.accept_tokens` attempts to advance grammar FSM over `<tool_call>` and fails\n\nThis is unavoidable when a reasoning end marker can also be part of the grammar:\n- We must not constrain any reasoning end marker because it forces the model to end reasoning, changing the output distribution\n- We must constrain any token that's part of the grammar.\nWe can't satisfy both requirements with implicit reasoning ends\n\n### Proposed Change.\n\nAs I see it, the only way to avoid this is disallow implicit reasoning markers. SGLang has a feature `--enable-strict-thinking` that \"Blocks model-specific excluded tokens (e.g., tool call markers) during reasoning. Requires a grammar backend that supports token filtering.\" https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/server_arguments\n\nI see two ways to implement this:\n1. Global implementation that reads a model's implicit reasoning end marker and disallow them during sampling\n    - Con: Doesn't work for models with multi-token reasoning end markers. Additional logic to maintain.\n2. Per-model structural tags (via the structural tags registry)\n    - Con: Reliance on xgrammar, doesn't work with other backends\n\nQuestions for maintainers:\n1. Do we want to add a `--enable-strict-thinking` feature to cover the reamining edge case?\n2. If so, do we prefer a global implementation or per-model structural tags?\n3. If not, do we have preferences on how to address remaining edge cases (multi-token / text only reasoning end, non engine-parsers)\n\n\n### Feedback Period.\n\n_No response_\n\n### CC List.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Any Other Things.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60722/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61330","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61330/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61330/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61330/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/61330","id":5824658528,"node_id":"I_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABWy08YA","number":61330,"title":"[Bug]: DFlash speculative decoding with gpt-oss target crashes with FA3 illegal memory access","user":{"login":"oscarw-td","id":318511979,"node_id":"U_kgDOEvwbaw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/318511979?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td","html_url":"https://github.com/oscarw-td","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarw-td/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5135047172,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABMhKaBA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6915642480,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABnDRUcA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/speculative-decoding","name":"speculative-decoding","color":"6A493C","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9089517981,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAACHccJnQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/gpt-oss","name":"gpt-oss","color":"10A37F","default":false,"description":"Related to GPT-OSS models","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-13T04:44:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T23:34:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Your current environment\n\n<details>\n<summary>The output of <code>python collect_env.py</code></summary>\n\n```text\nCollecting environment information...\nuv is set\n==============================\n        System Info\n==============================\nOS                           : Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (x86_64)\nGCC version                  : (Ubuntu 15.2.0-16ubuntu1) 15.2.0\nClang version                : Could not collect\nCMake version                : version 4.2.3\nLibc version                 : glibc-2.43\n\n==============================\n       PyTorch Info\n==============================\nPyTorch version              : 2.13.0+cu130\nIs debug build               : False\nCUDA used to build PyTorch   : 13.0\nROCM used to build PyTorch   : N/A\nXPU used to build PyTorch    : N/A\n\n==============================\n      Python Environment\n=================