                : Could not collect\nvLLM Version                 : 0.31.1rc1.dev23+g43b4aaea3 (git sha: 43b4aaea3)\nvLLM Build Flags:\n  CUDA Archs: 7.5 8.0 8.6 8.9 9.0 10.0 12.0; ROCm: Disabled; XPU: Disabled\nGPU Topology:\n  \tGPU0\tGPU1\tGPU2\tGPU3\tCPU Affinity\tNUMA Affinity\tGPU NUMA ID\nGPU0\t X \tNODE\tNV11\tSYS\t0-31,64-95\t0\t\tN/A\nGPU1\tNODE\t X \tNODE\tSYS\t0-31,64-95\t0\t\tN/A\nGPU2\tNV11\tNODE\t X \tSYS\t0-31,64-95\t0\t\tN/A\nGPU3\tSYS\tSYS\tSYS\t X \t32-63,96-127\t1\t\tN/A\n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\n==============================\n     Environment Variables\n==============================\nNVIDIA_REQUIRE_CUDA=cuda>=13.0 brand=unknown,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=grid,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=tesla,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=nvidia,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=quadro,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=quadrortx,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=nvidiartx,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=vapps,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=vpc,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=vcs,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=vws,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=cloudgaming,driver>=535,driver<536 brand=unknown,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=grid,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=tesla,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=nvidia,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=quadro,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=quadrortx,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=nvidiartx,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=vapps,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=vpc,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=vcs,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=vws,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=cloudgaming,driver>=550,driver<551 brand=unknown,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=grid,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=tesla,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=nvidia,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=quadro,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=quadrortx,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=nvidiartx,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=vapps,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=vpc,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=vcs,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=vws,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=cloudgaming,driver>=565,driver<566 brand=unknown,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=grid,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=tesla,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=nvidia,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=quadro,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=quadrortx,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=nvidiartx,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=vapps,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=vpc,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=vcs,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=vws,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=cloudgaming,driver>=570,driver<571 brand=unknown,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=grid,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=tesla,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=nvidia,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=quadro,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=quadrortx,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=nvidiartx,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=vapps,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=vpc,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=vcs,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=vws,driver>=575,driver<576 brand=cloudgaming,driver>=575,driver<576\nCUDA_VERSION=13.0.2\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/nvidia/lib64:/usr/local/cuda/lib64:/usr/local/cuda/lib64:/usr/local/nvidia/lib:/usr/local/nvidia/lib64:/usr/local/cuda/lib64\nNVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=compute,utility\nCUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda\nCUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda\nVLLM_ENABLE_CUDA_COMPATIBILITY=0\nTORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=7.5 8.0 8.6 8.9 9.0 10.0 12.0\nVLLM_USAGE_SOURCE=production-docker-image\nVLLM_BUILD_COMMIT=43b4aaea3e40e20ef53ce2bfecfa1b72060bf2b5\nVLLM_BUILD_PIPELINE=019d130e-464e-4ff7-b84b-492992c0c06b\nVLLM_BUILD_URL=https://buildkite.com/vllm/release-v2/builds/7908\nVLLM_IMAGE_TAG=vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-43b4aaea3e40e20ef53ce2bfecfa1b72060bf2b5\nCUDA_DEVICE_SM_LIMIT=100\nCUDA_DEVICE_MEMORY_SHARED_CACHE=/usr/local/vgpu/1603d8d3-47dc-4872-b165-7438c4e416b8.cache\nCUDA_DEVICE_MEMORY_LIMIT_0=40960m\nCUDA_DEVICE_MEMORY_LIMIT_1=40960m\nCUDA_DEVICE_MEMORY_LIMIT_2=40960m\nCUDA_DEVICE_MEMORY_LIMIT_3=40960m\nPYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True\nCUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID\nVLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1\nNVIDIA_CTK_LIBCUDA_DIR=/usr/lib64\nNVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=void\nPYTORCH_NVML_BASED_CUDA_CHECK=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_COMPILE_THREADS=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/torchinductor_vllm\n```\n\n</details>\n\nCollected with `python -m vllm.collect_env` inside the image where the failure happened (`vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-43b4aaea3`, 4x A100-PCIE-40GB). The code involved is unchanged in v0.32.0 and in `main` at 371745e.\n\n\n### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nSince #59533 (merged on 2026-10-05, first released in v0.32.0), Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (`Qwen4Exp`) checkpoints that quantize the full-attention `q_proj`/`k_proj`/`v_proj` but keep the QSA indexer projection `indexer.index_qk_proj` unquantized no longer load. Model construction stops at the first QSA layer:\n\n```text\nValueError: Found different quantization schemes for the shards of language_model.model.layers.3.self_attn.qkv_proj. vLLM requires all to use the same scheme.\n```\n\nBefore #59533 the indexer projection was a separate layer, so these checkpoints loaded. The checkpoint below was validated by its author on vLLM 0.29.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```bash\nvllm serve ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-AWQ \\\n  --revision 598afc96128f76a67117caf878f538d34f6f1e02 \\\n  --tensor-parallel-size 4 --enable-expert-parallel\n```\n\n- The checkpoint is compressed-tensors W4A16 (`pack-quantized`, `targets: [\"Linear\"]`). Its `ignore` list contains `model.language_model.layers.<N>.self_attn.indexer.index_qk_proj` for every QSA layer.\n- We ran it on 4x A100-40GB with more serving flags (context length, KV cache, multimodal limits). The error is raised while the layers are constructed, before any weights are loaded, so those flags should not matter.\n- Adding `--enable-lora --max-loras 1 --max-lora-rank 8` gives the same error at the same line.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full traceback (one TP worker; all four workers are identical)</summary>\n\n```text\nWorkerProc failed to start.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py\", line 915, in worker_main\n    worker = WorkerProc(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/tracing/otel.py\", line 175, in sync_wrapper\n    return func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py\", line 682, in __init__\n    self.worker.load_model()\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py\", line 575, in load_model\n    self.model_runner.load_model(load_dummy_weights=load_dummy_weights)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py\", line 385, in load_model\n    self.model = model_loader.load_model(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/tracing/otel.py\", line 175, in sync_wrapper\n    return func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/base_loader.py\", line 75, in load_model\n    model = self.create_model(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/base_loader.py\", line 52, in create_model\n    model = initialize_model(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/tracing/otel.py\", line 175, in sync_wrapper\n    return func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/utils.py\", line 96, in initialize_model\n    model = model_class(vllm_config=vllm_config, prefix=prefix)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py\", line 956, in __init__\n    self.language_model = Qwen4ExpForCausalLM(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py\", line 655, in __init__\n    self.model = Qwen4ExpModel(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py\", line 393, in __init__\n    self.start_layer, self.end_layer, self.layers = make_layers(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/models/utils.py\", line 905, in make_layers\n    + get_offloader().wrap_modules(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/offloader/base.py\", line 120, in wrap_modules\n    return list(modules_generator)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/models/utils.py\", line 906, in <genexpr>\n    layer_fn(prefix=f\"{prefix}.{idx}\") for idx in range(start_layer, end_layer)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py\", line 387, in get_layer\n    return Qwen4ExpDecoderLayer(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py\", line 227, in __init__\n    self.self_attn = Qwen4ExpQSAAttention(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py\", line 409, in __init__\n    self.qkv_proj = QKVParallelLinear(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/linear.py\", line 1067, in __init__\n    super().__init__(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/linear.py\", line 502, in __init__\n    super().__init__(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/linear.py\", line 290, in __init__\n    elif quant_method := resolve_quant_method(quant_config, self, prefix=prefix):\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/base_config.py\", line 306, in resolve_quant_method\n    base_quant_method = quant_config.get_quant_method(layer, prefix)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/compressed_tensors.py\", line 160, in get_quant_method\n    quant_scheme = self.get_scheme(layer=layer, layer_name=prefix)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/compressed_tensors.py\", line 922, in get_scheme\n    scheme_dict = self.get_scheme_dict(layer, layer_name)\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/compressed_tensors.py\", line 968, in get_scheme_dict\n    if should_ignore_layer(\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/utils.py\", line 66, in should_ignore_layer\n    raise ValueError(\nValueError: Found different quantization schemes for the shards of language_model.model.layers.3.self_attn.qkv_proj. vLLM requires all to use the same scheme.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### Root cause\n\n1. `Qwen4ExpForCausalLM.packed_modules_mapping[\"qkv_proj\"]` includes `indexer.index_qk_proj` ([model.py#L704](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.32.0/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py#L704)). `Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration` reuses it.\n2. `configure_quant_config` gives this class-level dict to the quant config before the model is built ([model_loader/utils.py#L88](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.32.0/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/utils.py#L88), [#L381](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.32.0/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/utils.py#L381)).\n3. So even the plain `QKVParallelLinear` at [qsa.py#L410](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.32.0/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py#L410), built before any fusion, is checked as a four-shard fused layer. compressed-tensors sees q/k/v quantized and the indexer ignored, and raises ([compressed_tensors/utils.py#L67](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.32.0/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/utils.py#L67)). `is_layer_skipped` in `quantization/utils/quant_utils.py` and `is_layer_gptq_quantized` in `quantization/utils/gptq_utils.py` have the same \"all shards same precision\" check, so GPTQ, AutoRound and FP8 checkpoints with this layout probably fail the same way (not tested).\n4. The LoRA branch ([model.py#L724-L727](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.32.0/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py#L724-L727)) rebinds `self.packed_modules_mapping` on the instance, but the quant config keeps the class dict from step 2. That is why `--enable-lora` does not avoid the error, although the indexer is not fused in that mode.\n\nModelOpt FP4 is already special-cased with `without_modelopt_fp4`. Other formats are not.\n\nChanging the checkpoint's `ignore` list does not help. It describes how the weights are stored (q/k/v packed INT4, `index_qk_proj` BF16). The fourth shard comes from vLLM's `packed_modules_mapping`, not from the checkpoint.\n\n### Scope\n\nWe read `model.safetensors.index.json` of the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next quantized checkpoints on the Hub (2026-10-18). In 26 of the 82 quantized (non-GGUF, non-MLX) checkpoints we could inspect, layer 3 `q_proj`/`k_proj`/`v_proj` carry quantization tensors and `index_qk_proj` has only `.weight`. Examples with compressed-tensors and the indexer in `ignore`:\n\n- `davetha/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DERISKED-W4A16-AWQ`\n- `VnimanieAI/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16`\n- `primitive-ai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-mixed-NVFP4-FP8`\n- `ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-AWQ`\n\n`Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8` and `nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4` leave attention unquantized and are not affected.\n\n### Workaround we use\n\nA runtime patch sets `packed_modules_mapping[\"qkv_proj\"]` to `[\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"v_proj\"]` on both model classes and turns `fuse_indexer_projection` off. With it, the Swift checkpoint loads on 4x A100-40GB (TP4 + EP) and passes our functional and speed smoke tests. The indexer then runs as its own GEMM, as before #59533.\n\n### Proposed fix\n\nFuse the indexer into `qkv_proj` only when `q_proj`/`k_proj`/`v_proj` and `index_qk_proj` resolve to the same quantization. Otherwise keep the indexer as its own layer, and give the quant config a packed mapping that matches that decision (per model instance, not the class dict). This also fixes the `--enable-lora` path.\n\nI would like to send a PR for this. @gau-nernst, does this direction fit #59533, or do you prefer another approach?\n\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62308/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62308/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62277","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62277/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62277/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62277/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62277","id":5908418832,"node_id":"I_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABYCtREA","number":62277,"title":"[Bug]: Cold-cache KV cache OOM with `--kv-cache-memory-bytes` and `--enable-sleep-mode`","user":{"login":"maxtonhuang","id":68006265,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MDA2MjY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68006265?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang","html_url":"https://github.com/maxtonhuang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maxtonhuang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5135047172,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABMhKaBA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-18T10:06:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T10:06:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Your current environment\n\nRTX 5090 32 GB (SM120), driver 617.14, Windows 11 + WSL2 (Ubuntu 26.04), torch 2.13.0+cu130, FlashInfer 0.7.0.post1, vLLM nightly `0.32.0rc1.dev35+g656d0d450`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>vllm collect-env</summary>\n\n```text\nCollecting environment information...\n==============================\n        System Info\n==============================\nOS                           : Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS (x86_64)\nGCC version                  : (Ubuntu 15.2.0-16ubuntu1) 15.2.0\nClang version                : Could not collect\nCMake version                : Could not collect\nLibc version                 : glibc-2.43\n\n==============================\n       PyTorch Info\n==============================\nPyTorch version              : 2.13.0+cu130\nIs debug build               : False\nCUDA used to build PyTorch   : 13.0\nROCM used to build PyTorch   : N/A\nXPU used to build PyTorch    : N/A\n\n==============================\n      Python Environment\n==============================\nPython version               : 3.12.14 (main, Sep 24 2026, 17:57:43) [Clang 22.1.3 ] (64-bit runtime)\nPython platform              : Linux-6.18.33.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2-x86_64-with-glibc2.43\n    \n==============================\n       CUDA / GPU Info\n==============================\nIs CUDA available            : True\nCUDA runtime version         : Could not collect\nCUDA_MODULE_LOADING set to   : \nGPU models and configuration : GPU 0: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090\nNvidia driver version        : Could not collect\ncuDNN version                : Could not collect\nHIP runtime version          : N/A\nMIOpen runtime version       : N/A\nIs XNNPACK available         : False\n\n==============================\n          CPU Info\n==============================\nArchitecture:                            x86_64\nCPU op-mode(s):                          32-bit, 64-bit\nAddress sizes:                           48 bits physical, 48 bits virtual\nByte Order:                              Little Endian\nCPU(s):                                  32\nOn-line CPU(s) list:                     0-31\nVendor ID:                               AuthenticAMD\nModel name:                              AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor\nCPU family:                              26\nModel:                                   68\nThread(s) per core:                      2\nCore(s) per socket:                      16\nSocket(s):                               1\nStepping:                                0\nBogoMIPS:                                8599.81\nFlags:                                   fpu vme de pse tsc msr pae mce cx8 apic sep mtrr pge mca cmov pat pse36 clflush mmx fxsr sse sse2 ht syscall nx mmxext fxsr_opt pdpe1gb rdtscp lm constant_tsc rep_good nopl xtopology tsc_reliable nonstop_tsc cpuid extd_apicid tsc_known_freq pni pclmulqdq ssse3 fma cx16 sse4_1 sse4_2 movbe popcnt aes xsave avx f16c rdrand hypervisor lahf_lm cmp_legacy svm cr8_legacy abm sse4a misalignsse 3dnowprefetch osvw topoext perfctr_core ssbd ibrs ibpb stibp vmmcall fsgsbase bmi1 avx2 smep bmi2 erms invpcid avx512f avx512dq rdseed adx smap avx512ifma clflushopt clwb avx512cd sha_ni avx512bw avx512vl xsaveopt xsavec xgetbv1 xsaves avx_vnni avx512_bf16 clzero xsaveerptr arat npt nrip_save tsc_scale vmcb_clean flushbyasid decodeassists pausefilter pfthreshold v_vmsave_vmload avx512vbmi umip avx512_vbmi2 gfni vaes vpclmulqdq avx512_vnni avx512_bitalg avx512_vpopcntdq rdpid fsrm avx512_vp2intersect\nVirtualization:                          AMD-V\nHypervisor vendor:                       Microsoft\nVirtualization type:                     full\nL1d cache:                               768 KiB (16 instances)\nL1i cache:                               512 KiB (16 instances)\nL2 cache:                                16 MiB (16 instances)\nL3 cache:                                96 MiB (1 instance)\nNUMA node(s):                            1\nNUMA node0 CPU(s):                       0-31\nVulnerability Gather data sampling:      Not affected\nVulnerability Ghostwrite:                Not affected\nVulnerability Indirect target selection: Not affected\nVulnerability Itlb multihit:             Not affected\nVulnerability L1tf:                      Not affected\nVulnerability Mds:                       Not affected\nVulnerability Meltdown:                  Not affected\nVulnerability Mmio stale data:           Not affected\nVulnerability Old microcode:             Not affected\nVulnerability Reg file data sampling:    Not affected\nVulnerability Retbleed:                  Not affected\nVulnerability Spec rstack overflow:      Vulnerable: Safe RET, no microcode\nVulnerability Spec store bypass:         Mitigation; Speculative Store Bypass disabled via prctl\nVulnerability Spectre v1:                Mitigation; usercopy/swapgs barriers and __user pointer sanitization\nVulnerability Spectre v2:                Mitigation; Retpolines; IBPB conditional; IBRS_FW; STIBP always-on; RSB filling; PBRSB-eIBRS Not affected; BHI Not affected\nVulnerability Srbds:                     Not affected\nVulnerability Tsa:                       Not affected\nVulnerability Tsx async abort:           Not affected\nVulnerability Vmscape:                   Not affected\n\n==============================\nVersions of relevant libraries\n==============================\n[pip3] flashinfer-python==0.7.0.post1\n[pip3] nccl-extensions==0.1.0\n[pip3] nccl4py==0.6.0\n[pip3] numpy==2.3.5\n[pip3] nvidia-cublas==13.1.1.3\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-cccl==13.3.4.3.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-crt==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-cupti==13.0.85\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvcc==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-nvrtc==13.0.88\n[pip3] nvidia-cuda-runtime==13.0.96\n[pip3] nvidia-cudnn-cu13==9.20.0.48\n[pip3] nvidia-cudnn-frontend==1.31.0\n[pip3] nvidia-cufft==12.0.0.61\n[pip3] nvidia-cufile==1.15.1.6\n[pip3] nvidia-curand==10.4.0.35\n[pip3] nvidia-cusolver==12.0.4.66\n[pip3] nvidia-cusparse==12.6.3.3\n[pip3] nvidia-cusparselt-cu13==0.8.1\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl==4.8.0\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-base==4.8.0\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-core==4.8.0\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu12==4.8.0\n[pip3] nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-cu13==4.8.0\n[pip3] nvidia-ml-py==13.615.71\n[pip3] nvidia-nccl-cu13==2.29.7\n[pip3] nvidia-nvjitlink==13.4.92\n[pip3] nvidia-nvshmem-cu13==3.4.5\n[pip3] nvidia-nvtx==13.0.85\n[pip3] nvidia-nvvm==13.4.92\n[pip3] pyzmq==27.2.0\n[pip3] tokenspeed-triton==3.9.10.post20261008\n[pip3] torch==2.13.0+cu130\n[pip3] torch_c_dlpack_ext==0.1.5\n[pip3] torchaudio==2.11.0+cu130\n[pip3] torchcodec==0.17.0+cu130\n[pip3] torchvision==0.28.0+cu130\n[pip3] transformers==5.19.0\n[pip3] triton==3.7.1\n[conda] Could not collect\n\n==============================\n         vLLM Info\n==============================\nROCM Version                 : Could not collect\nvLLM Version                 : 0.32.0rc1.dev35+g656d0d450 (git sha: 656d0d450)\nvLLM Build Flags:\n  CUDA Archs: Not Set; ROCm: Disabled; XPU: Disabled\nGPU Topology:\n  Could not collect\n\n==============================\n     Environment Variables\n==============================\nPYTORCH_NVML_BASED_CUDA_CHECK=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_COMPILE_THREADS=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/torchinductor_<user>\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/<user>/llm/.venv-nvfp4kv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/cv2/../../lib64:\nVLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn\n```\n</details>\n\n### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\n**Problem.** With `--kv-cache-memory-bytes` and `--enable-sleep-mode`, a start with empty compile caches (first start after install or upgrade) of the command below fails while allocating the KV cache (`allocate_kv_cache`, `vllm/v1/worker/utils.py`):\n\n```text\ntorch.OutOfMemoryError: CUDA out of memory. Tried to allocate 4.46 GiB. GPU 0 has a total capacity of 31.82 GiB of which 946.25 MiB is free. Of the allocated memory 26.80 GiB is allocated by PyTorch, with 4.76 GiB allocated in private pools (e.g., CUDA Graphs), and 2.35 GiB is reserved by PyTorch but unallocated.\n```\n\nWith warm caches the same command started in our tests, so the failure looks intermittent. Seen with both `--kv-cache-dtype fp8` and `nvfp4`. The model's weights are NVFP4, which is where the buffer below comes from; other weight formats were not tested, but the missing guards are not format-specific. v0.31.0 also lacks both in this branch (not run).\n\n**Cause.** The `kv_cache_memory_bytes` branch of `Worker.determine_available_memory()` runs `profile_run()` without either allocator guard that the memory-profiling branch has:\n\n1. **No cache release.** `memory_profiling` runs `gc.collect()` and `empty_cache()` on exit; this branch does not, so fully free cached segments (2.4 GiB here) stay reserved. The open PR #59893 adds this release.\n2. **No split limit.** #58430 runs the memory-profiling `profile_run()` inside `_scoped_allocator_max_split(max_split_size_mb=20)`; this branch does not. A snapshot just before KV allocation (both instrumented unpatched cold starts) showed a 2,426 MiB segment kept reserved by a single live 40 MiB FlashInfer scratch buffer (`flashinfer/utils.py` `_get_cache_buf`, from `mm_fp4`). `empty_cache()` cannot release that segment while the scratch buffer remains live; with #59893 alone, device-free memory also stayed lower after start-up and after a 10,408-token request.\n\nWith sleep mode the KV cache is allocated in the separate CuMem pool, so these retained default-pool reservations reduce the device memory available to it. `VLLM_ENABLE_STARTUP_PLAN=1` also sets `kv_cache_memory_bytes` (from a saved plan), so those starts take the same branch.\n\n**Fix.** #59893 plus the split limit on the same `profile_run()` (`vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py`, on top of #59893):\n\n```diff\n         if kv_cache_memory_bytes := self.cache_config.kv_cache_memory_bytes:\n             # still need a profile run which compiles the model for\n             # max_num_batched_tokens\n-            with set_current_vllm_config(self.vllm_config):\n+            # Same allocator split limit as the memory-profiling branch below.\n+            with (\n+                self._scoped_allocator_max_split(max_split_size_mb=20),\n+                set_current_vllm_config(self.vllm_config),\n+            ):\n                 self.model_runner.profile_run(\n                     randomize_inputs=self.randomize_dummy_inputs\n                 )\n```\n\n#59893's test then needs the real scope on its stand-in worker (one statement, in the suggestion on that PR). With both, `tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_worker.py` passes on main `1b2a666` (26 tests, including #59893's GPU test), and so do vLLM's pre-commit hooks. The suggested source and test changes are posted on #59893; this report does not propose a separate PR.\n\n**Verification** (vLLM nightly `0.32.0rc1.dev35+g656d0d450`). `unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4`, 4.5 GiB KV budget, sleep mode. All rows used empty vLLM, inductor and Triton cache folders; in the last two rows, every start also completed a short request and a 10,408-token prompt:\n\n| | KV dtype | Starts | Free before KV allocation | Free after the 10K request | Engine init | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Unpatched | fp8 / nvfp4 | 3 / 1 | 3.49 GiB (2 measured) | - | - | OOM every time |\n| Split limit only | fp8 / nvfp4 | 3 / 2 | 4.59 to 4.66 GiB | - | - | Starts |\n| #59893 only | fp8 / nvfp4 | 2 / 2 | 5.79 to 5.81 GiB | 1.02 to 1.09 GiB | 94.2 to 107.6 s | Starts, serves |\n| #59893 + split limit | fp8 / nvfp4 | 1 / 1 | 8.64 GiB | 2.15 to 2.27 GiB | 73.8 to 74.4 s | Starts, serves |\n\nThe last two rows were measured on the same day, with about 0.81 GiB of other GPU usage before start-up; engine-init times are as observed, not explained. The same code with a different comment wording also started 5 of 5 cold starts (fp8 2, nvfp4 3) with 8.64 GiB free before KV allocation. The open PR #56698 also avoided this OOM in our tests: it removes this branch, so pinned sizes are profiled and checked against an estimate; it targets a different failure (a pin too large for the activation peak).\n\nRelated but distinct: #54122 and #54209 concern cold-compilation peaks inflating activation estimates on the `--gpu-memory-utilization` path. The pinned path skips that sizing calculation, and #54209 resets peak counters without releasing cached memory or preventing live scratch buffers from pinning segments.\n\nWorkaround until fixed: `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=max_split_size_mb:20` (CUDA graph memory rose from 0.25 to 2.42 GiB here).\n\n**Reproduce.**\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /tmp/cold/vllm /tmp/cold/inductor /tmp/cold/triton\nVLLM_CACHE_ROOT=/tmp/cold/vllm TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/cold/inductor TRITON_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/cold/triton \\\nvllm serve unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 --max-model-len 98304 --kv-cache-dtype fp8 \\\n  --kv-cache-memory-bytes 4831838208 --max-num-batched-tokens 4096 --max-cudagraph-capture-size 32 \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\": \"mtp\", \"num_speculative_tokens\": 3}' \\\n  --enable-sleep-mode --language-model-only --max-num-seqs 2\n```\n\nUse new empty folders for each attempt; with warm caches it started in our tests.\n\nBackground: found while testing NVFP4 KV cache on SM120 (#46963, #60452). On v0.30.0, FP8 was the smallest KV cache type on this GPU; NVFP4 fits 54% to 57% more tokens in the same budget (Qwen3.8-27B: 109,794 to 169,082; Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: 157,640 to 248,200).\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code, reviewed by Codex) was used for the investigation, the tests and this write-up.\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62277/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60581","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60581/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60581/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60581/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60581","id":5758973653,"node_id":"I_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABV0L21Q","number":60581,"title":"[Usage]: ROCm gfx950: MXFP4 activation quant not fused into GEMM; Quark INT4 W4A16 uses a very slow Triton kernel","user":{"login":"fyun89","id":26920538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTIwNTM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26920538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89","html_url":"https://github.com/fyun89","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fyun89/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6114440385,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABbHL0wQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/rocm","name":"rocm","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Related to AMD ROCm","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6697501599,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABjzPDnw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/usage","name":"usage","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"How to use vllm","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-08T09:02:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T08:39:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Your current environment\n\n```text\nCollecting environment information...\n==============================\n        System Info\n==============================\nOS                           : Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS (x86_64)\nGCC version                  : (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04.3) 11.4.0\nClang version                : 22.0.0git (https://github.com/RadeonOpenCompute/llvm-project roc-7.2.3 26084 f58b06dce1f9c15707c5f808fd002e18c2accf7e)\nCMake version                : version 3.31.10\nLibc version                 : glibc-2.35\n\n==============================\n       PyTorch Info\n==============================\nPyTorch version              : 2.13.0+git733fca1\nIs debug build               : False\nCUDA used to build PyTorch   : N/A\nROCM used to build PyTorch   : 7.2.53211\nXPU used to build PyTorch    : N/A\n\n==============================\n      Python Environment\n==============================\nPython version               : 3.12.15 (main, Oct  1 2026, 15:41:07) [GCC 11.4.0] (64-bit runtime)\nPython platform              : Linux-6.8.0-146-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.35\n\n==============================\n       CUDA / GPU Info\n==============================\nIs CUDA available            : True\nCUDA runtime version         : Could not collect\nCUDA_MODULE_LOADING set to   :\nGPU models and configuration :  (gfx950:sramecc+:xnack-)\nNvidia driver version        : Could not collect\ncuDNN version                : Could not collect\nHIP runtime version          : 7.2.53211\nMIOpen runtime version       : 3.5.1\nIs XNNPACK available         : False\n\n==============================\n          CPU Info\n==============================\nArchitecture:                            x86_64\nCPU op-mode(s):                          32-bit, 64-bit\nAddress sizes:                           52 bits physical, 57 bits virtual\nByte Order:                              Little Endian\nCPU(s):                                  48\nOn-line CPU(s) list:                     0-47\nVendor ID:                               AuthenticAMD\nModel name:                              AMD Ryzen Threadripper 7960X 24-Cores\nCPU family:                              25\nModel:                                   24\nThread(s) per core:                      2\nCore(s) per socket:                      24\nSocket(s):                               1\nStepping:                                1\nCPU max MHz:                             5665.0000\nCPU min MHz:                             545.0000\nBogoMIPS:                                8387.04\nFlags:                                   fpu vme de pse tsc msr pae mce cx8 apic sep mtrr pge mca cmov pat pse36 clflush mmx fxsr sse sse2 ht syscall nx mmxext fxsr_opt pdpe1gb rdtscp lm constant_tsc rep_good amd_lbr_v2 nopl nonstop_tsc cpuid extd_apicid aperfmperf rapl pni pclmulqdq monitor ssse3 fma cx16 pcid sse4_1 sse4_2 x2apic movbe popcnt aes xsave avx f16c rdrand lahf_lm cmp_legacy svm extapic cr8_legacy abm sse4a misalignsse 3dnowprefetch osvw ibs skinit wdt tce topoext perfctr_core perfctr_nb bpext perfctr_llc mwaitx cpb cat_l3 cdp_l3 hw_pstate ssbd mba perfmon_v2 ibrs ibpb stibp ibrs_enhanced vmmcall fsgsbase bmi1 avx2 smep bmi2 erms invpcid cqm rdt_a avx512f avx512dq rdseed adx smap avx512ifma clflushopt clwb avx512cd sha_ni avx512bw avx512vl xsaveopt xsavec xgetbv1 xsaves cqm_llc cqm_occup_llc cqm_mbm_total cqm_mbm_local user_shstk avx512_bf16 clzero irperf xsaveerptr rdpru wbnoinvd amd_ppin cppc amd_ibpb_ret arat npt lbrv svm_lock nrip_save tsc_scale vmcb_clean flushbyasid decodeassists pausefilter pfthreshold avic vgif x2avic v_spec_ctrl vnmi avx512vbmi umip pku ospke avx512_vbmi2 gfni vaes vpclmulqdq avx512_vnni avx512_bitalg avx512_vpopcntdq la57 rdpid overflow_recov succor smca fsrm flush_l1d debug_swap ibpb_exit_to_user\nVirtualization:                          AMD-V\nL1d cache:                               768 KiB (24 instances)\nL1i cache:                               768 KiB (24 instances)\nL2 cache:                                24 MiB (24 instances)\nL3 cache:                                128 MiB (4 instances)\nNUMA node(s):                            1\nNUMA node0 CPU(s):                       0-47\nVulnerability Gather data sampling:      Not affected\nVulnerability Indirect target selection: Not affected\nVulnerability Itlb multihit:             Not affected\nVulnerability L1tf:                      Not affected\nVulnerability Mds:                       Not affected\nVulnerability Meltdown:                  Not affected\nVulnerability Mmio stale data:           Not affected\nVulnerability Reg file data sampling:    Not affected\nVulnerability Retbleed:                  Not affected\nVulnerability Spec rstack overflow:      Mitigation; Safe RET\nVulnerability Spec store bypass:         Mitigation; Speculative Store Bypass disabled via prctl\nVulnerability Spectre v1:                Mitigation; usercopy/swapgs barriers and __user pointer sanitization\nVulnerability Spectre v2:                Mitigation; Enhanced / Automatic IBRS; IBPB conditional; STIBP always-on; PBRSB-eIBRS Not affected; BHI Not affected\nVulnerability Srbds:                     Not affected\nVulnerability Tsa:                       Mitigation; Clear CPU buffers\nVulnerability Tsx async abort:           Not affected\nVulnerability Vmscape:                   Mitigation; IBPB before exit to userspace\n\n==============================\nVersions of relevant libraries\n==============================\n[pip3] conch-triton-kernels==1.2.1\n[pip3] numpy==2.3.5\n[pip3] onnx==1.22.0\n[pip3] onnx-ir==1.0.0\n[pip3] onnxscript==0.7.2\n[pip3] onnxslim==0.1.97\n[pip3] pyzmq==27.2.0\n[pip3] torch==2.13.0+git733fca1\n[pip3] torch_c_dlpack_ext==0.1.5\n[pip3] torchaudio==2.11.0+34c52a6\n[pip3] torchvision==0.28.0+8fb8771\n[pip3] transformers==5.19.0\n[pip3] triton==3.8.0+git669b31ac\n[conda] Could not collect\n\n==============================\n         vLLM Info\n==============================\nROCM Version                 : 7.2.53211-c2d9476115\nvLLM Version                 : 0.31.1rc1.dev88+g81198e97b (git sha: 81198e97b)\nvLLM Build Flags:\n  CUDA Archs: Not Set; ROCm: Disabled; XPU: Disabled\nGPU Topology:\n  ============================ ROCm System Management Interface ============================\n================================ Weight between two GPUs =================================\n       GPU0\nGPU0   0\n\n================================= Hops between two GPUs ==================================\n       GPU0\nGPU0   0\n\n=============================== Link Type between two GPUs ===============================\n       GPU0\nGPU0   0\n\n======================================= Numa Nodes =======================================\nGPU[0]          : (Topology) Numa Node: 0\nGPU[0]          : (Topology) Numa Affinity: -1\n================================== End of ROCm SMI Log ===================================\n\n==============================\n     Environment Variables\n==============================\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/rocm/lib:/usr/local/lib:\nPYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH=gfx90a;gfx942;gfx950;gfx1100;gfx1101;gfx1200;gfx1201;gfx1150;gfx1151\nMAX_JOBS=16\nPYTORCH_NVML_BASED_CUDA_CHECK=1\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0\nTORCHINDUCTOR_COMPILE_THREADS=1\nTORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/torchinductor_root\n```\nQwen3.8-27B on MI350P, vLLM 0.31.1rc1.dev88, AITER enabled.\n(a) AiterMxfp4LinearKernel quantizes activations in a separate kernel before each GEMM:\n    309 launches, 1.2 ms of a ~10.6 ms step at c=1 (decode TPOT 9.5 ms, mem% ~40%).\n    gemm_with_dynamic_quant is opaque to the compiler even with fuse_norm_quant on. Fusing would cut ~1 ms.\n(b) amd/Qwen3.8-27B-Quark-AWQ-INT4-W4A16 runs triton_w4a16_gemm_kernel at ~261 us per GEMM:\n    TPOT 82 ms vs 9.5 ms for the MXFP4 checkpoint, mem% ~5%. A fast gfx950 W4A16 path is needed.\n\n### How would you like to use vllm\n\nI'm serving Qwen3.8-27B (amd/Qwen3.8-27B-Quark-AWQ-MXFP4) on a single AMD Instinct MI350P (gfx950, 128 CUs)\nwith vLLM 0.31.1rc1.dev88 (vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly) for low-latency single-user and small-batch\ndecode (c=1 to ~32), with image input enabled. Current command:\n\nvllm serve /model --served-model-name amd/Qwen3.8-27B-Quark-AWQ-MXFP4 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.88 --max-model-len 32768 --max-num-seqs 32 \\\n  --max-num-batched-tokens 16384 --kv-cache-dtype fp8 \\\n  --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\": 3, \"video\": 0}'\n(env: VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FP4_ASM_GEMM=1)\n\nMeasured on this card: mean TPOT 9.5 ms at c=1, 10.7 ms at c=8, 13.0 ms at c=32. A profile shows decode is bound by\nkernel launches rather than HBM bandwidth (mem% ~40%): the MXFP4 linear path quantizes activations in a separate\nkernel before every GEMM (309 launches, ~1.2 ms of ~10.6 ms per step). I'd like to use fused activation quant + GEMM\nhere, and a fast W4A16 path on gfx950 (the Quark INT4 W4A16 checkpoint currently falls back to triton_w4a16_gemm_kernel\nat ~261 us per GEMM, TPOT 82 ms).\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/60581/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62264","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62264/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62264/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62264/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/62264","id":5907331687,"node_id":"I_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABYBq6Zw","number":62264,"title":"[Bug]: --attention-backend b12x fails at startup without --block-size (impl checks block size before the platform applies the preferred one)","user":{"login":"VidyasagarDudekula","id":56215798,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjE1Nzk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56215798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula","html_url":"https://github.com/VidyasagarDudekula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VidyasagarDudekula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-18T07:40:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T07:40:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Your current environment\n\n<details>\n<s